  "question": {
    "text": "If the tangent at a point on the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>27</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> meets the coordinate axes at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is the origin, then the minimum area (in sq. units) of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
